WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.885
This example creates two useful outputs at the same
time First we

00:00:05.911 --> 00:00:11.029
create a preferred contact method We normalize blank
values and use email

00:00:11.196 --> 00:00:15.694
mobile phone and home phone in that order Second we
create a

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:20.926
billing category Notice that missing bill amounts
become Needs review rather than

00:00:20.951 --> 00:00:25.694
being placed into the Low Value category An exact
zero becomes No

00:00:25.719 --> 00:00:32.468
Charge Then we apply the High Value and Standard
thresholds The

00:00:32.481 --> 00:00:36.787
SQL is available below Run it in the browser and
study the

00:00:36.812 --> 00:00:42.084
preferred contact and billing tier columns You can
also use Copy and

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:47.728
run it in pgAdmin The important design idea is that
presentation

00:00:47.754 --> 00:00:52.408
defaults should not hide data-quality problems A
missing bill is not the

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.967
same thing as a small bill
